WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.700
Part two: finding a shift and signing up.

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:11.377
Scroll down to the shifts. Pick a day: setup is Friday, the contest is Saturday, and teardown is Sunday.

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:23.660
Contest-day shifts are grouped in blocks, like Early and Late. Exact times come once the contest schedule is out. Each block shows how many spots are open. Tap it to open it.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:28.521
Each station shows how many spots are open, and who's already on it.

00:00:28.721 --> 00:00:30.535
Tap Sign up on the one you want.

00:00:30.735 --> 00:00:37.100
Some spots are filled by the coordinators. Part five shows how to put your name in for those.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:47.220
Then tap who's working it. Only people who can take that spot show up. It checks age, group, and anything they're already doing at that time.

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:50.140
That's it. It's saved right away.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.133
What your family owes updates,

00:00:52.333 --> 00:00:55.070
and the shift shows up under Your shifts.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.779
Looking for something specific? Open Filter.

00:00:58.979 --> 00:01:01.049
Tap stations to show just those.

00:01:01.249 --> 00:01:04.002
Or show only the spots that still have openings.

00:01:04.202 --> 00:01:08.880
Expand all and Collapse all open or close every block at once.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:15.840
Next, in part three: your shifts, your point person, and reminders on your phone's calendar.
